==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-ptg|pt}} {{term|novo|lang=roa-ptg}}, from {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|novus||new|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|pt}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*néwos||new}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|PT|Brazil}} {{IPA|/ˈno.vu/|lang=pt}}
* {{audio|Pt novo.ogg|Audio}}
* {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|/ˈno.vo/|lang=pt}}

===Adjective===
{{pt-adj|nov|o}}

# {{l/en|new}} {{gloss|recently made or created}}
#: {{usex|É uma casa '''nova'''.|t=It is a '''new''' house.|lang=pt}}
# {{l/en|new}} {{gloss|not previously worn or used}}
#: {{usex|Comprei um carro '''novo'''.|t=I bough a '''new''' car.|lang=pt}}
# {{l/en|new}} {{gloss|recently discovered}}
#: {{usex|As '''novas''' ruínas serão úteis aos arqueólogos.|t=The '''new''' ruins will be useful to archaeologists.|lang=pt}}
# {{l/en|new}}; {{l/en|young}}
#: {{usex|Ele é '''novo''' demais para assistir isso.|t=He is too '''young''' to watch this.|lang=pt}}
# {{l/en|original}} {{gloss|fresh; different}}
#: {{usex|Ideias '''novas''' para tempos novos.|t='''Original''' ideas for new times.|lang=pt}}
# {{context|of a period of time|often follows the noun|lang=pt}} {{l/en|new}} {{gloss|about to begin or recently begun}}
#: {{usex|Ano '''novo'''.|t='''New''' year.|lang=pt}}

====Inflection====
{{pt-adj infl|nov|o}}

====Synonyms====
